---
layout: base.njk
title: Questions
permalink: /questions/
description: Who can apply, what a grant can pay for, and how the process goes. Plain answers.
items:
  - id: who
    q: Who can apply?
    a: Eligible applicants are 501(c)(3) organizations seeking support for church bells and bell towers, pipe organs, rose windows, stained glass, related sacred architecture, artisan training, and, in some cases, spiritual work with sound, color, and frequency. Grants are made case by case. We focus on Christian sacred spaces, with room for related work.
  - id: where
    q: Do you fund projects outside the United States?
    a: Not yet. For now we are concentrating on projects in the United States. International work may follow later, through other 501(c)(3) organizations.
  - id: size
    q: How large is a grant?
    a: Grant amounts are discussed directly with applicants after review. Every project is different, so every grant is set case by case, according to the need and the funds we have available.
  - id: what
    q: What can a grant pay for, and what can it not?
    a: Bells and their towers, pipe organs, rose windows and stained glass, and the training of the artisans who keep them. It cannot pay salaries, operating costs or debt, general building work unrelated to bells, organs or glass, or anything political. The full lists are on the guidelines page.
  - id: nobells
    q: Our church has no bells. Can we still apply?
    a: Yes. An electronic carillon brings the true sound of cast bronze bells through speakers in a steeple or on an exterior wall — nothing to cast, nothing to build. It rings the Call to Worship and the Angelus, peals for weddings and tolls for funerals, and its library holds thousands of hymns, Ave Maria and Gregorian chant among them. Ask for one in your inquiry.
  - id: how
    q: How do I apply?
    a: Send a short inquiry through the form on this site. It takes a few minutes and asks for no documents. If it looks like a fit, we will write back and ask for photographs, drawings and estimates.
  - id: decides
    q: Who decides, and how long does it take?
    a: The board reviews requests as they are received. If a request proceeds past the first review, we will ask for additional materials. Timing varies.
  - id: deadline
    q: Is there a deadline?
    a: No. Inquiries are welcome at any time of year, and we read them as they arrive.
---
<section class="section section--hero">
  <div class="content stack">
    <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
    <h1 class="display">Questions</h1>
    <p class="lede">Plain answers. If yours is not here, write to us and a person will reply.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap faq" data-faq>
    <div class="faq__list" role="list">
      {%- for item in items %}
      <div class="faq__item" role="listitem" data-faq-item>
        <h2 class="faq__q">
          <button class="faq__bar" type="button" id="faq-{{ item.id }}" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-{{ item.id }}-body" data-faq-bar>
            <span>{{ item.q }}</span>
            <i class="ph ph-arrow-right icon icon--sm faq__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="faq__body" id="faq-{{ item.id }}-body" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-{{ item.id }}" data-faq-body>
          <p>{{ item.a }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
      <div class="faq__item faq__item--ask" role="listitem" data-faq-item>
        <h2 class="faq__q">
          <button class="faq__bar" type="button" id="faq-ask" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ask-body" data-faq-bar>
            <span>Ask a question of your own</span>
            <i class="ph ph-arrow-right icon icon--sm faq__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="faq__body" id="faq-ask-body" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-ask" data-faq-body>
          <p>If your question is not on this page, ask it here. A person reads every message and writes back.</p>
          <form class="faq__ask" data-ask-form novalidate>
            <div class="grid grid--form">
              <div class="field">
                <label for="ask-name">Your name</label>
                <div><input class="field__control" id="ask-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="ask-email">Email<span class="field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
                <div><input class="field__control" id="ask-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="ask-q">Your question<span class="field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
              <div><textarea class="field__control" id="ask-q" name="question" rows="4" required></textarea></div>
              <span class="field__error" data-ask-error hidden></span>
            </div>
            <div><button class="btn" type="submit">Send the question</button></div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq__detail" data-faq-panel aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
  </div>
</section>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for item in items %}
    { "@type": "Question", "name": {{ item.q | dump | safe }}, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | dump | safe }} } }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>
